  "text": {
    "intro": "The Thornwood Knitting Circle meets weekly and has not agreed on anything since 1998.\nFive knitters are involved. Determine each knitter's day and yarn.\n- **Knitter**: Willem, Maddie, Ebba, Angus and Serafina.\n- **Day** (listed from earlier to later): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday and Friday.\n- **Yarn**: mohair of great expense, nettle fiber, mill-end acrylic, undyed Shetland and recycled sari silk.\nEvery knitter has a different day and yarn, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "Ebba knits on Tuesday.",
      "Serafina knits on Friday.",
      "Maddie knits on Thursday.",
      "The knitter who works in recycled sari silk knits on Tuesday. The knitter who works in mill-end acrylic does not knit on Monday.",
      "Ebba is exactly one day earlier than the knitter who works in mohair of great expense, with no day in between.",
      "Angus is exactly one day earlier than the knitter who works in nettle fiber, with no day in between."
    ]
  }
